  "_comment": "Reviewed concept bridges: a job description's phrasing on the left, the literal industry/candidate wording that genuinely satisfies that concept on the right. Every entry is a literal phrase checked with the same word-boundary test as every other alias -- this is NOT fuzzy matching. A bridge only changes which PHRASES are searched for; it never asserts that the candidate has the skill. The same form list is used against the resume AND against master evidence, so a bridge can surface real evidence the resume words differently, but it can never manufacture support that the evidence bank does not contain: a concept whose bridged forms appear in the resume but in no evidence record is reported as resume-claim-without-evidence (ambiguous), not as covered. Rule for adding one: the right-hand phrase must be a genuine name for the left-hand concept, or a specific instance of it. Non-equivalent technologies must never bridge to each other.",

