  "_v869_comment": "Bridges below added in V8.6.9, narrowed in V8.6.10 after review against this file's own rule. Each right-hand phrase was checked against terminology that actually appears in evidence records, not invented from a job description. IMPORTANT and easy to get wrong: these forms are matched against the resume AND against master evidence, so a bridge DOES affect the ATS gate. It cannot invent an evidence record, but a bridge that is too broad can let a loosely-related evidence phrase satisfy a concept it does not really support, which raises coverage against the gate threshold. That is why entries here must instantiate the left-hand concept rather than merely relate to it -- broadening a bridge is a change to gate behaviour, not just to reporting.",

